    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-07-10 is anchored by high-ceiling matchups against soft-throwing rotations. **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) remains our premier daily play; he faces a favorable 4.91 xERA matchup and benefits from a significant 16% park factor boost and dynamic platoon advantages, easily offsetting the slight drag caused by an elite hold-pitcher scenario. Joining him at the top of the production hierarchy are **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.41) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a strong 16% SP skill advantage against the lefty, while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill lift and a 13% platoon edge. Furthermore, **Andy Pages** (74.01) and **Josh Lowe** (68.71) are high-priority targets due to their utility in the stolen base category; both face pitchers with slow deliveries, creating a situational efficiency boost that enhances their value in our 5x5 build.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Heliot Ramos** (54.25), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Heliot Ramos** offers an enticing 10% order bonus and favorable wind conditions, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor and superior matchup context of **Sam Antonacci** and **Brayan Rocchio**. Despite a negative platoon shift, **Sam Antonacci** secured a starting spot on the strength of a 19% SP skill advantage. We are closely monitoring the status of **Kyle Tucker**, **Cole Carrigg**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Heliot Ramos**, as their lineups remain pending; any downward shifts in their projected batting order could trigger a bench shuffle. **Miguel Vargas** remains a high-value sleeper in the utility slot, as his elite 0.402 xwOBA suggests he could easily outperform his 63.53 score if he finds the gaps against the vulnerable Lopez.",
